        /// <summary>
        /// Upload To Pixeldrain ### Overview  Uploads a file, or a zip of a whole download, from your TorBox account to Pixeldrain. Send the &#x60;id&#x60; of the torrent, usenet download or web download, its &#x60;type&#x60;, either the &#x60;file_id&#x60; of one file or &#x60;zip&#x60; set to true, and the API key of the Pixeldrain account to upload to in &#x60;pixeldrain_token&#x60;.  The route accepts a request without &#x60;pixeldrain_token&#x60;, but nothing can be uploaded without one: the job then fails with the detail \&quot;No API key provided. Please provide an API key to upload to Pixeldrain.\&quot; Only the key sent in the request is used.  The route answers at once with a &#x60;job_id&#x60;. The upload itself runs in the background as a transfer job, and nothing is checked with Pixeldrain before the answer, so a key Pixeldrain does not accept only shows up as a failed job. Follow the job with Get Specific Job (&#x60;/v1/api/integration/job/{job_id}&#x60;), Get All Jobs (&#x60;/v1/api/integration/jobs&#x60;) or Get All Jobs By Hash (&#x60;/v1/api/integration/jobs/{hash}&#x60;), and stop it with Cancel Specific Job.  The job goes from \&quot;pending\&quot; through \&quot;preparing\&quot; and \&quot;uploading\&quot; to \&quot;completed\&quot; or \&quot;failed\&quot;. Its &#x60;detail&#x60; says what it is doing or why it failed, and its &#x60;progress&#x60; runs from 0 to 1. When it is completed, its &#x60;download_url&#x60; is the Pixeldrain link of the file (&#x60;https://pixeldrain.com/u/...&#x60;) and you get an \&quot;Upload Complete\&quot; notification. A failed job is deleted about an hour after it failed, a completed job about 7 days after it completed.  A file of 100 GB (107,374,182,400 bytes) or more is not uploaded: the request is queued and the job fails. The download has to be cached on TorBox, otherwise the job fails. Send &#x60;file_id&#x60; or &#x60;zip&#x60;: with neither there is no file to upload and the job never completes.  ### Authorization  Requires an API key using the Authorization Bearer Header. 
